title: EMR Connect › Sync › What other screens use from EMR Connect
route: /emr
intro: Two other screens lean on EMR Connect: New case can pull a chart, and the Dashboard can write an approval back. In the demo neither one reads this page's systems or switches.
dir: TD
also: Found by reading the code and testing the built demo. Disconnect every system and 'Pull' in New case still works.
---
screen p1 "EMR Connect\nSystems, sync, mappings and the write-back switch"

group gPull "New case: pull a chart"
  click a1 "Click 'Pull a chart from EMR Connect'"
  overlay a2 "Chart from EMR Connect\nDropdown with four charts, a hint under each"
  input a3 "Pick a chart\nJ.M., 34 · Summit · Residential 3.5 (Admitted yesterday)\nA.R., 45 · Beacon · IOP (Intake on Thursday)\nS.T., 38 · Harborview · PHP (In program, day 9)\nL.G., 29 · Cardinal · Residential 3.5 (Admission tomorrow)"
  click a4 "Click 'Pull'\nOr 'Cancel'"
  process a5 "Button reads 'Pulling' for one second"
  store a6 "Case draft is filled in\nPatient, payer, member ID, level of care, request type, diagnoses, reason"
  toast a7 "'Pulled J.M., 34 from EMR Connect'\n'Everything below was filled in from the chart. You can still change it.'"
endgroup
process n1 "The four charts are a fixed list\nNot read from the systems on this page, and not changed by Sync now or by Disconnect"
goto g1 "Continues in: Authorizations › New case › Medical records › Patient and insurance rows"
group gWrite "Dashboard: write back"
  screen b1 "Dashboard request: 'Approved. Write-back waits for you'"
  click b2 "Click 'Approve write-back'"
  overlay b3 "Approve the write-back\n'EMR Connect will write only these three things to the chart. No notes, diagnoses or identifiers are written.'"
  process b4 "Approval number, approved amount and dates are listed"
  click b5 "Click 'Write to the EMR'\nOr 'Cancel'"
  ext b6 "The record system receives the three values\nDemo: simulated, about one second"
  store b7 "Request gets 'You confirmed the write-back' and a Cadence event\nToast: 'Written to the EMR'"
endgroup
process n2 "The per-system write-back switch in Manage is not checked here\nThe modal opens whether it is on or off"
goto g2 "Continues in: Dashboard › Request drawer › Approve the write-back"

p1 -.-> a1
a1 --> a2 --> a3 --> a4 --> a5 --> a6 --> a7
a2 -.-> n1
n1 --> g1
p1 -.-> b1
b1 --> b2 --> b3 --> b4 --> b5 --> b6 --> b7
b3 -.-> n2
n2 --> g2
